{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-107550","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173438","text":"SpecPrompt"}]},{"id":"blk-107551","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173439","text":"Content-addressed identity for specifications — a spec whose name is a hash of what it says, so changing the claim changes the name. Elixir/OTP with a Phoenix API and an MCP server. Part of the "},{"id":"spn-173440","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://computedriven.com"}],"text":"ComputeDriven"},{"id":"spn-173441","text":" world."}]},{"id":"blk-107552","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173442","marks":["bold"],"text":"Written 2026-08-16."},{"id":"spn-173443","text":" This repository had no README before that date. Every figure below was measured that day with the command beside it."}]},{"id":"blk-107553","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173444","text":"Status, honestly"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-107555","spans":[{"id":"spn-173445","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-107556","spans":[{"id":"spn-173446","text":""}]}],"id":"blk-107554","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-107557","spans":[{"id":"spn-173447","text":"Version"}]},{"id":"blk-107558","spans":[{"id":"spn-173448","marks":["code"],"text":"0.1.0"},{"id":"spn-173449","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-173450","marks":["code"],"text":"mix.exs"},{"id":"spn-173451","text":", app "},{"id":"spn-173452","marks":["code"],"text":":specprompt"},{"id":"spn-173453","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-107559","spans":[{"id":"spn-173454","text":"Tests"}]},{"id":"blk-107560","spans":[{"id":"spn-173455","marks":["bold"],"text":"93 passing, 0 failures"},{"id":"spn-173456","text":" — 71 Elixir ("},{"id":"spn-173457","marks":["code"],"text":"mix test"},{"id":"spn-173458","text":") + 22 TypeScript ("},{"id":"spn-173459","marks":["code"],"text":"npx vitest run"},{"id":"spn-173460","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-173461","marks":["code"],"text":"npm/"},{"id":"spn-173462","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-107561","spans":[{"id":"spn-173463","text":"Marketing page"}]},{"id":"blk-107562","spans":[{"id":"spn-173464","marks":["bold"],"text":"live"},{"id":"spn-173465","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-173466","marks":["code"],"text":"https://specprompt.com"},{"id":"spn-173467","text":" answers 200"}]}],[{"id":"blk-107563","spans":[{"id":"spn-173468","text":"Application"}]},{"id":"blk-107564","spans":[{"id":"spn-173469","marks":["bold"],"text":"live on Fly"},{"id":"spn-173470","text":" as app "},{"id":"spn-173471","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt"},{"id":"spn-173472","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-173473","marks":["code"],"text":"https://app.specprompt.com"},{"id":"spn-173474","text":" answers 200"}]}],[{"id":"blk-107565","spans":[{"id":"spn-173475","text":"Evidence rung"}]},{"id":"blk-107566","spans":[{"id":"spn-173476","marks":["code"],"text":"live_deployed"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-107567","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173477","marks":["bold"],"text":"Correction, 2026-08-17 — 71 and 93 are both right, of different things, and this file used to say one of them was wrong."},{"id":"spn-173478","text":" It read "},{"id":"spn-173479","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"The test count is 71, not 93 … the suite says 71\""},{"id":"spn-173480","text":". Re-derived by running both suites: "},{"id":"spn-173481","marks":["code"],"text":"mix test"},{"id":"spn-173482","text":" prints "},{"id":"spn-173483","marks":["bold"],"text":"71 tests, 0 failures"},{"id":"spn-173484","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-173485","marks":["code"],"text":"npx vitest run"},{"id":"spn-173486","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-173487","marks":["code"],"text":"npm/"},{"id":"spn-173488","text":" prints "},{"id":"spn-173489","marks":["bold"],"text":"22 passed"},{"id":"spn-173490","text":". 71 + 22 = "},{"id":"spn-173491","marks":["bold"],"text":"93"},{"id":"spn-173492","text":". The plan's figure was the whole repository and "},{"id":"spn-173493","marks":["code"],"text":"mix test"},{"id":"spn-173494","text":" is the Elixir half of it — a scope collision, not a stale number, and the same shape as the 103-vs-118 law counts on "},{"id":"spn-173495","marks":["code"],"text":"opensentience.org"},{"id":"spn-173496","text":". The earlier diagnosis would have made the landing page understate itself by 22 tests."}]},{"id":"blk-107568","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173497","marks":["bold"],"text":"Never hand-type either number."},{"id":"spn-173498","text":" "},{"id":"spn-173499","marks":["code"],"text":"build-site.mjs"},{"id":"spn-173500","text":" executes both runners on every build, parses what they print, and refuses to emit the landing page if a count has moved off "},{"id":"spn-173501","marks":["code"],"text":"records/tests.json"},{"id":"spn-173502","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-107569","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173503","marks":["bold"],"text":"What is live is the prior design."},{"id":"spn-173504","text":" The marketing page describes content-addressed spec identity. What is deployed predates that, which is why the portfolio nav carries "},{"id":"spn-173505","marks":["code"],"text":"status: \"live · prior design\""},{"id":"spn-173506","text":" rather than \"shipped\". It runs; it is not yet the thing the page describes."}]},{"id":"blk-107570","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173507","text":"Two modes, and only one of them is superseded"}]},{"id":"blk-107571","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173508","text":"The spec defines a "},{"id":"spn-173509","marks":["bold"],"text":"filesystem mode"},{"id":"spn-173510","text":" (git-based, no database, auth-optional, for local CLI use) and a "},{"id":"spn-173511","marks":["bold"],"text":"registry mode"},{"id":"spn-173512","text":" (multi-tenant, Supabase-backed). This distinction matters more here than in the sibling repositories:"}]},{"id":"blk-107572","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107574","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173513","marks":["bold"],"text":"Filesystem mode is unaffected"},{"id":"spn-173514","text":" by the data-layer ruling. It commits to git"}]}],"id":"blk-107573","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-107575","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173515","text":"and needs no database at all."}]},{"id":"blk-107576","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107578","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173516","marks":["bold"],"text":"Registry mode rests on the abandoned shared-Supabase layer"},{"id":"spn-173517","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-173518","marks":["code"],"text":"spec.specs"},{"id":"spn-173519","text":","}]}],"id":"blk-107577","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-107579","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173520","text":"workspace scoping, "},{"id":"spn-173521","marks":["code"],"text":"amp.profiles"},{"id":"spn-173522","text":" identity via Supabase Auth."}]},{"id":"blk-107580","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173523","text":"Quick start"}]},{"id":"blk-107581","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"mix deps.get\nmix compile --warnings-as-errors\nmix test                       # 71 tests\nmix format --check-formatted\nmix phx.server"},{"id":"blk-107582","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173524","text":"Deploy is "},{"id":"spn-173525","marks":["code"],"text":"fly deploy"},{"id":"spn-173526","text":" against "},{"id":"spn-173527","marks":["code"],"text":"fly.toml"},{"id":"spn-173528","text":" (app "},{"id":"spn-173529","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt"},{"id":"spn-173530","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-107583","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173531","text":"The deployed MCP endpoint answers on "},{"id":"spn-173532","marks":["code"],"text":"POST /mcp"},{"id":"spn-173533","text":". Note it is content-type particular — a bare JSON-RPC POST without the accept header it wants returns "},{"id":"spn-173534","marks":["bold"],"text":"406"},{"id":"spn-173535","text":", which is the app refusing the request rather than failing to serve it."}]},{"id":"blk-107584","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173536","text":"The specification is authoritative, and superseded in part"}]},{"id":"blk-107585","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173537","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/spec/README.md"},{"id":"spn-173538","text":" (v1.1, dated February 2026) drives implementation. It carries a supersession banner added 2026-08-15:"}]},{"id":"blk-107586","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107588","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173539","marks":["bold"],"text":"Superseded:"},{"id":"spn-173540","text":" §5.2's Supabase schema, the "},{"id":"spn-173541","marks":["code"],"text":"workspace_id"},{"id":"spn-173542","text":" multi-tenancy,"}]}],"id":"blk-107587","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-107589","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173543","marks":["code"],"text":"supabase://auth"},{"id":"spn-173544","text":" as the identity source — everything in registry mode that rests on the shared data layer abandoned by ruling on "},{"id":"spn-173545","marks":["bold"],"text":"2026-07-30"},{"id":"spn-173546","text":". The replacement, "},{"id":"spn-173547","marks":["code"],"text":"studbook"},{"id":"spn-173548","text":", is a spec with no implementation and is blocked on an unruled confidentiality question. "},{"id":"spn-173549","marks":["bold"],"text":"Do not build against it yet."}]},{"id":"blk-107590","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107592","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173550","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not superseded:"},{"id":"spn-173551","text":" the content-addressing design, the spec identity model, the"}]}],"id":"blk-107591","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-107593","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173552","text":"filesystem mode, and the CLI. That is the part worth reading."}]},{"id":"blk-107594","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173553","text":"The spec was "},{"id":"spn-173554","marks":["bold"],"text":"not rewritten"},{"id":"spn-173555","text":". It is a dated design record and rewriting it would fabricate a review nobody performed."}]},{"id":"blk-107595","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173556","text":"A standing direction that affects this repository"}]},{"id":"blk-107596","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173557","text":"Ruled 2026-08-15: "},{"id":"spn-173558","marks":["bold"],"text":"compute moves into the ComputeDriven OS, and the Fly.io apps become storage or nothing."},{"id":"spn-173559","text":" This app is one of them. Nothing is torn down before its OS-side replacement runs locally, but check "},{"id":"spn-173560","marks":["code"],"text":"STACK_HUB.md"},{"id":"spn-173561","text":" in the workspace before planning new Fly-shaped work."}]},{"id":"blk-107597","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173562","text":"The portfolio nav"}]},{"id":"blk-107598","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173563","marks":["code"],"text":"amp-nav.js"},{"id":"spn-173564","text":" is a "},{"id":"spn-173565","marks":["bold"],"text":"deployed copy"},{"id":"spn-173566","text":". The source is "},{"id":"spn-173567","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand-nav/src/amp-nav.js"},{"id":"spn-173568","text":", fanned out by "},{"id":"spn-173569","marks":["code"],"text":"sync-nav.sh"},{"id":"spn-173570","text":". Edits here are lost on the next sync."}]},{"id":"blk-107599","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173571","text":"Conventions"}]},{"id":"blk-107600","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107602","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173572","marks":["code"],"text":"mix format"},{"id":"spn-173573","text":", warnings-as-errors."}]}],"id":"blk-107601","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107604","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173574","text":"Never commit secrets."}]}],"id":"blk-107603","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107606","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173575","marks":["code"],"text":"old_scrap/"},{"id":"spn-173576","text":" is historical and not authoritative."}]}],"id":"blk-107605","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-107607","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173577","text":"Related"}]},{"id":"blk-107608","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107610","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173578","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://computedriven.com"}],"text":"computedriven.com"},{"id":"spn-173579","text":" — the discipline this is built under"}]}],"id":"blk-107609","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107612","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173580","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://fleetprompt.com"}],"text":"fleetprompt.com"},{"id":"spn-173581","text":" — the registry that installs what this names"}]}],"id":"blk-107611","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107614","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173582","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://bendscript.com"}],"text":"bendscript.com"},{"id":"spn-173583","text":" — graph-first documents, which reference this"}]}],"id":"blk-107613","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107616","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173584","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://ampersandboxdesign.com"}],"text":"ampersandboxdesign.com"},{"id":"spn-173585","text":" — the [&] Protocol"}]}],"id":"blk-107615","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieralckov7hnwzwyzxnnom6ofq4mhywzxyzaaibqh5fdfponhnqmqkbq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}